## Linked issue

Closes nibiru-labs/openbot-roadmap#62 (M10 accessibility, audit `docs/audits/openbot-a11y.md`, all 15 findings).

## Type of change

- [x] Bug fix
- [ ] Small improvement or alignment, with no change to how a feature works
- [ ] New provider, MCP app, or connector
- [ ] Translation or documentation
- [ ] New feature or change to existing behavior (needs an approved issue)

## What changed

- Shared keyboard helper (Shift+F10 / ContextMenu key) on every context menu trigger; the free-area menu and Mark all read have a keyboard path (1, 15).
- Chats in a sidebar section move with Alt+ArrowUp/Down (2). Sidebar rows put chat state and unread count into the accessible name (3).
- The selection toolbar takes focus on open and returns it on dismiss (4). Tab triggers without panels became radio groups (5).
- The planner shows routine status as text (6). Five toolbars use a shared roving tabindex with arrow keys (7). Onboarding focus order matches the visual order (8).
- Pinned tile reorder publishes `aria-keyshortcuts` (9). Nine toggles carry `aria-controls` (10). Four dialog triggers report `aria-expanded` (11).
- The tab close hint uses `aria-describedby` (12). Diagram and preview canvases use `role=group` instead of `application` (13). The switch field reads label first (14).

Surfaces: Desktop renderer and `packages/ui` shared controls. Mouse behavior and visuals are unchanged. No IPC, contract or migration change; new text comes from `@openbot/i18n`.

## Verification

- [x] `bun run typecheck:renderer` and `bun run check:ui` passed for every run on the executor hosts (rc 0).
- [x] Keyboard behavior is covered by the checks in the PR; broad checks run in CI.
- [x] The pre-commit hook passed.
- [x] No credentials, private data, generated output, or real user files are included.

## Risk and security impact

UI only. The shared keyboard helper sits on every context menu trigger, so it is the part to review for focus handling.

Model and harness: Codex gpt-6.1-terra, Cursor composer-2.5 and pi + MiniMax through openswarm; planner Claude Code.

